cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GoalGA in your work, please cite it with the metadata below and also cite the paper whose model it
  implements (listed under "references").
title: "GoalGA: goal-based dynamic asset allocation with genetic algorithms"
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "DaValz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaValz/goalga"
abstract: >-
  A guided, multilingual robo-advisor that finds the glide path of nine efficient portfolios most likely to reach a
  set of financial goals, using a genetic algorithm on bootstrapped market scenarios. It implements the model of
  Pomante, Farina and Cucurachi (2024) and adds out-of-sample verification, a seeded universe of ~3,500 funds and
  stocks, accounts with weight-change alerts and a Streamlit interface.
keywords:
  - goal-based investing
  - dynamic asset allocation
  - glide path
  - genetic algorithm
  - robo-advisor
  - Streamlit
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A “Plug-and-Play,” Goal-Based, Dynamic Asset Allocation Model with Genetic Algorithms"
    authors:
      - family-names: Pomante
        given-names: Ugo
      - family-names: Farina
        given-names: Vincenzo
      - family-names: Cucurachi
        given-names: Paolo Antonio
    journal: "The Journal of Wealth Management"
    volume: 26
    issue: "4"
    start: 33
    end: 48
    year: 2024
    doi: "10.3905/jwm.2024.1.227"
    url: "https://doi.org/10.3905/jwm.2024.1.227"
